(label "VBAT_SENSE" (at 322.58 58.42 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "9985268a-cf8c-4e83-998d-8420d11ccfae"))
(text "POWER: 1S LiPo -> VBAT (motors direct) / MT3608 module -> +5V. Power off = unplug J1\n!! Adjust MT3608 to 5.0V with a multimeter BEFORE plugging the MCU module" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20.32 38.1 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "75bc6818-7475-4896-a97e-f3cff644f623"))
(text "VBAT sense: 10k/10k -> PF0 (ADC0), 4.2V -> 2.1V" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20.32 66.04 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "040fe8f5-7701-4442-88ec-25d1317cdbb8"))
(text "MOTOR DRIVER x4: SI2302 low-side, SS14 flyback across motor, gate 100R series + 10k pulldown" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20.32 116.84 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "98f3ff88-d3dd-4a45-ad9c-038ae0068f51"))
(text "PERIPHERALS (plug-in modules)\nHC-06: TX -> RXD1 direct, RXD1 <- TXD1 via 1k/2k (5V -> 3.3V). Check module pin order (VCC/GND/TXD/RXD) before PCB\nGY-521: 5V in (onboard LDO + I2C pullups), AD0 onboard pulldown -> addr 0x68" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20.32 195.58 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "8d604037-3963-4967-85a2-f9b66539bda9"))
(text "MCU: AT128A-70B V2.0 on 2x 1x29 female headers (do not solder the module)\nPF4-PF7 = JTAG (onboard 4.7k pullups), PE0/PE1/PB1 = ISP -> left unused" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 248.92 38.1 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "484efbc9-9366-42e5-a5be-231284e511ac"))
(text "C5/C6: bulk + decoupling\nat module VCC header" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 243.84 111.76 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "b87a8e14-12d3-4e83-b758-ad769d450022"))
(text "PIN MAP\nPB5/PB6/PB7 = OC1A/B/C -> M1/M2/M3 PWM\nPE3 = OC3A -> M4 PWM\nPE4 = INT4 <- ECHO,  PE5 -> TRIG\nPE6 = INT6 <- MPU-6050 INT\nPD0/PD1 = SCL/SDA (TWI)\nPD2/PD3 = RXD1/TXD1 (USART1, also module USART conn)\nPF0 = ADC0 <- VBAT/2\n\nWIRED BACKUP (AR-UART2USB): plug into the module's own\nUSART connector (same USART1). Remove HC-06 first and\nleave the red 5V wire unconnected (board has its own 5V)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 332.74 132.08 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "a7929549-3967-4a45-8af3-48cbd71c8ca4"))
